LookPath semantics, read against Go 1.26.6 os/exec (lp_windows.go, exec.go): a path with separators goes lookPathExts -> findExecutable: PATHEXT appended when there is no extension, no PATH search, and ErrDot cannot occur (only the bare-name branch sets it; the k119 branch of warnIfMissing is unchanged). exec.Command resolves the same way: absolute -> lookExtensions(name, "") -> lookPathExts; relative with separators -> lookExtensions(path, cmd.Dir) at Start, and the ue service sets no Dir, so cwd-relative like LookPath. A path that already has .exe is stat-checked (exists: no warning; missing: warns). Simulating the copied separator branch on Linux confirmed: .../UE_5.4/.../UnrealEditor -> UnrealEditor.exe (a dot in a parent directory does not count as an extension), a directory and an existing extension-less file -> not found. The side effect is right: exec cannot start a directory or an extension-less file either. One divergence, negligible: for a path whose extension is in PATHEXT, lookExtensions returns it unchecked while LookPath also tries X.exe.exe.
